{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Fibre laser welding of 6082-T6 butt joints: screening plan",
  "notes": "Screening plan for autogenous fibre laser welding of 3 mm 6082-T6 aluminium butt joints (6 kW fibre laser, Ø0.3 mm fibre, 200 mm welds, coupons cleaned and degreased within 4 h before welding). In the definitive screening design, main effects are unaliased with two-factor interactions and curvature is detectable. Joint gap is measured with feeler gauges at three positions per coupon and the ambient humidity in the cell is read from the logger at the start of each weld; enter both before analysing. Penetration and porosity come from one metallographic cross-section at mid-length, tensile strength from two transverse specimens per weld (ISO 4136).",
